  "description": "Normal-speed real-flow lifecycle trace for v20.1, hold-stage entry to full settle. Two complementary views: a fixed 200ms-interval sample (fine-grained, shows crossfade shape) and a state-driven per-continent-peak sample (labeled, used to pick the sequence screenshots). eye-gaze columns (holdRegionGazeX/Y) are derived from the recorded continent opacities using the same formula as the live code: holdEarthX = 0.75 + 0.25*emphX, inverted to recover emphX, then summed with the same directional weights used in render().",
  "methodology": "Real Playwright browser drive: page.goto -> window.showLogin() -> click .lp-dot[data-action=signin] -> poll for lhmz-stage-hold class -> sample opacities every ~200ms (interval trace) or on every poll tick until each continent/view condition is met (labeled trace) -> poll for lhmz-story-complete class. No fake timers used (page.clock breaks this animation's CSS-driven layout).",
